00:03:09.708 --> 00:03:10.908
- [Daniel] Alright, Believe Nation.

00:03:10.908 --> 00:03:12.636
Here's the first thing.

00:03:12.636 --> 00:03:13.977
You have to make sure

00:03:13.977 --> 00:03:17.208
that there is a demand
for your business, first,

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:19.208
because I think one of the biggest things,

00:03:19.208 --> 00:03:22.017
and actually, I'm at Fort Bragg right now,

00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:24.740
and so, I'm talking to veterans
about starting businesses,

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.927
and one of the big things
that they have trouble with,

00:03:27.927 --> 00:03:31.448
is thinking, man, if I leave the security

00:03:31.448 --> 00:03:34.359
of either, my job with the army,

00:03:34.359 --> 00:03:36.646
or some sort of regular nine-to-five job,

00:03:36.646 --> 00:03:38.187
I don't want to take the
risk of starting a business,

00:03:38.187 --> 00:03:39.316
'cause it could fail.

00:03:39.316 --> 00:03:41.110
And this is a problem
a lot of people have,

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.147
this mental barrier of, if
I start, it's going to fail.

00:03:43.147 --> 00:03:44.427
But, there are ways to make sure

00:03:44.427 --> 00:03:47.408
that it's a good idea, before
you invest time and money,

00:03:47.408 --> 00:03:49.048
and ways to, almost, invest no money.

00:03:49.048 --> 00:03:50.398
So, here's what I'd recommend.

00:03:50.398 --> 00:03:54.389
First of all, make sure that
the idea that you want to do

00:03:54.389 --> 00:03:56.484
is already being done by someone else,

00:03:56.484 --> 00:03:58.154
because that will give you, at least,

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:01.584
a decent amount of foresight
into what is, potentially,

00:04:01.584 --> 00:04:03.021
your level of success.

00:04:03.021 --> 00:04:05.047
What I like to do, and I'm just,

00:04:05.047 --> 00:04:07.127
I'm just being practical with this.

00:04:07.127 --> 00:04:09.156
I like to look at the things
that are already trending,

00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:10.764
and find a skill that I can pick,

00:04:10.764 --> 00:04:11.597
to start the business with.

00:04:11.597 --> 00:04:14.494
So, I'll go on somewhere, like...

00:04:14.494 --> 00:04:16.012
Well, now, it's called Upwork,

00:04:16.012 --> 00:04:17.979
and I'll look at all the
different things that they list,

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:22.760
everything from graphic
design, to video editing,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.616
to web development, to virtual assistant.

00:04:25.616 --> 00:04:27.705
And I'll see what types
of jobs are listed,

00:04:27.705 --> 00:04:30.556
and I'll think, which of these
skills would I like to learn?

00:04:30.556 --> 00:04:32.515
And I'll see that there
are multiple people asking

00:04:32.515 --> 00:04:33.348
for these things,

00:04:33.348 --> 00:04:35.002
or multiple people that are
paying for these services.

00:04:35.002 --> 00:04:36.918
I'll say, hey, there might
be a business model here,

00:04:36.918 --> 00:04:38.326
and rather than trying
to read about the wheel,

00:04:38.326 --> 00:04:40.244
I'll see what people are asking for first,

00:04:40.244 --> 00:04:41.538
and I'll make sure that there's a market,

00:04:41.538 --> 00:04:42.749
and then I'll go start it,

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.759
'cause I know that there's clients,

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:46.577
and a market base for it, first.

00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:47.719
- [Evan] Got it.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:48.640
- So, that's the first step,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.527
making sure that there's
a solid market for it.

00:04:50.527 --> 00:04:52.110
The next step is...

00:04:52.965 --> 00:04:56.888
Making sure that the market
actually has the amount

00:04:56.888 --> 00:04:58.194
of money that you want,

00:04:58.194 --> 00:05:00.356
to make sure that you can
make the type of money

00:05:00.356 --> 00:05:01.189
that you need.

00:05:01.189 --> 00:05:02.022
And, remember,

00:05:02.022 --> 00:05:02.890
that when you're first
starting your business,

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.389
and this is my philosophy, okay?

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:08.358
Everyone, if you talk to Mark Zuckerberg,

00:05:08.358 --> 00:05:09.658
he has a different philosophy.

00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:12.198
My philosophy, is start with
a service, because it's easy,

00:05:12.198 --> 00:05:13.448
and it's quick.

00:05:14.369 --> 00:05:15.919
So, I like to think, okay.

00:05:15.919 --> 00:05:17.321
What can I do now,

00:05:17.321 --> 00:05:19.332
to gradually replace
my nine-to-five income?

00:05:19.332 --> 00:05:20.511
So, I look at these jobs,

00:05:20.511 --> 00:05:22.040
let's say we're going back
to the Upwork example,

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.692
and I'm finding these skills,
I'm listing these things,

00:05:23.692 --> 00:05:25.401
I'm finding something that I
can do, and think to myself,

00:05:25.401 --> 00:05:27.163
alright, well, I see
that these jobs are going

00:05:27.163 --> 00:05:30.266
for like, maybe 500, to
a thousand dollars a job.

00:05:30.266 --> 00:05:31.179
Maybe, I can get a few of these,

00:05:31.179 --> 00:05:33.293
and it doesn't have to
be on the upper platform,

00:05:33.293 --> 00:05:36.027
but it can be, you can find
clients out in the wild.

00:05:36.027 --> 00:05:36.860
So, alright.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.826
If I can get a few of these clients...

00:05:39.826 --> 00:05:43.054
If I can start to pay for my
regular, day-to-day bills,

00:05:43.054 --> 00:05:47.425
with this side hustle work,
I can scale it up overtime.

00:05:47.425 --> 00:05:48.574
You don't need to quit your job,

00:05:48.574 --> 00:05:49.735
in order to start a new business.

00:05:49.735 --> 00:05:50.815
You can do both at the same time,

00:05:50.815 --> 00:05:51.883
and start something on the side,

00:05:51.883 --> 00:05:55.192
and then, once your side
income gets to about

00:05:55.192 --> 00:05:57.012
60, 70 percent of what your daily,

00:05:57.012 --> 00:05:58.620
like your monthly take-home is,

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.650
then, you're thinking to yourself,

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.891
oh, well, really, the only
thing holding me back now,

00:06:01.891 --> 00:06:03.069
is the time factor.

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:04.820
And since you're still putting
time into your nine-to-five,

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:08.091
you can eventually switch
gears, and move full-time,

00:06:08.091 --> 00:06:10.024
into whatever freelance business you pick.

00:06:10.024 --> 00:06:12.253
And then, the third thing
I would think about,

00:06:12.253 --> 00:06:13.864
when starting a new business,
to make sure it works,

00:06:13.864 --> 00:06:15.454
is what can you do differently, or better?

00:06:15.454 --> 00:06:17.872
So, let's say you went onto a job,

00:06:17.872 --> 00:06:19.184
