having been able to do this.

00:27:43.783 --> 00:27:45.365
And I always am setting new dreams.

00:27:45.365 --> 00:27:46.273
I don't have one.

00:27:46.273 --> 00:27:47.403
I don't want to be an astronaut.

00:27:47.403 --> 00:27:49.835
I don't have one big milestone in my life.

00:27:49.835 --> 00:27:53.443
I also don't think that's a
drawback, or to my detriment.

00:27:53.443 --> 00:27:55.063
I think it's great to have,

00:27:55.063 --> 00:27:56.746
like, one of my dreams is, for a summer,

00:27:56.746 --> 00:27:57.727
I want to be shredded.

00:27:57.727 --> 00:27:58.757
Is that not good enough?

00:27:58.757 --> 00:28:00.998
I want to just be jacked!

00:28:00.998 --> 00:28:04.562
I have little milestone
goals, milestone dreams.

00:28:04.562 --> 00:28:05.845
What's your big dream?

00:28:05.845 --> 00:28:06.803
Don't talk about my dream.

00:28:06.803 --> 00:28:08.521
What's your dream?

00:28:08.521 --> 00:28:09.551
- [Evan] Oh, flippin' it on 'em.

00:28:09.551 --> 00:28:10.384
I like it.

00:28:10.384 --> 00:28:11.217
- [Daniel] Flippin' it.

00:28:11.217 --> 00:28:12.050
- I like it, I like it.

00:28:12.050 --> 00:28:13.748
Cool, well, it's crazy how
quickly time goes, man!

00:28:13.748 --> 00:28:15.608
It's been awesome talkin' to you.

